==English==

===Etymology===
[[bahuvrihi|Bahuvrihi]] compound of {{compound|en|ass|wipe}}.  First use appears c. 1947 in the writings of {{w|Mari Sandoz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæswaɪp/|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|En-US-asswipe.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|North America|informal|vulgar}} An [[annoying]], [[contemptible]], or [[worthless]] person.
#: {{ux|en|He is such an '''asswipe'''!}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1996|author=Timothy Jay|title=What to Do When Your Students Talk Dirty|page=207|passage=...they have been exchanging insults in writing: "dickhead," "dillweed," "fuzzbutt," "dorkwad," "'''asswipe'''," and so forth.}}
# {{lb|en|North America|informal|vulgar|uncountable}} [[toilet paper|Toilet paper]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1976|author=Micheal Clodfelter|title=The Pawns of Dishonor|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=hffbAAAAIAAJ|page=249|publisher=Branden Press|isbn=9780828315876
|passage=I rapidly expended my own and everyone else’s supply of tiny [[w:Meal, Combat, Individual ration|C-ration]] rolls of '''asswipe''' and was reduced to wiping my nasty behind with leaves and grass.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|author=Nicholas Proffitt|title=Gardens of Stone|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=2FWxAAAAIAAJ|page=317|publisher=Carroll & Graf|isbn=9780881840179
|passage=“{{...}} Into your packs you put your toilet articles, mess kits, extra socks, and skivvies and longjohns if you have them. If you have a roll of '''asswipe''', put that in, too. {{...}}”<!-- [sic] quotation marks in original -->}}
#* '''2008''', Joseph Heywood, ''Death Roe: A Woods Cop Mystery'',<sup >[http://books.google.com/books?id=AQe3ujxs4VQC ][http://www.amazon.com/Death-Roe-Woods-Mystery-Mysteries/dp/1599214288 ]</sup> Globe Pequot, {{ISBN|9781599214283}}, page 252:
#*: “I doubt a dime would buy a single square of '''asswipe''' in this city, {{...}}” <!-- [sic] quotation marks in original -->

